;; goldragon — synchronizer configuration for the LiGoldragon kriom.
;; The synchronizer tool carries ZERO project data; every criome-specific
;; fact lives here. Schema: synchronizer SynchronizerConfig (positional,
;; untagged root). Canonical Nota: bare atoms for canonical strings,
;; brackets for lists, nested records for multi-field enum variants.
;;
;; Fields, in order:
;;   forge              (GitHub <owner>) — account holding every component remote
;;   checkout-root      absolute path holding the local component clones
;;   [component]        (<name> AtRoot | (AtPath <path>)) — participating repos
;;   branch-scheme      (<mainline> <staging>) — version target / tool-owned branch
;;   builder-resolution how the build-verify host is found:
;;                        (DirectHost <host>) — a literal host, or
;;                        (ClusterRole (<role> <cluster-source>)) — role via cluster
;;   verify-policy      (WireExercising [<word>]) — build checks whose name carries
;;                        a listed word, else the default package build; or
;;                        DefaultBuild — always the default `nix build`
;;   commit-author      (<name> <email>) — author/committer of every bump commit
;;
;; The cluster-role strategy resolves NixBuilder against this same repo's
;; datom.nota, so the config and the cluster proposal it reads version
;; together. sema-engine is deliberately out of the set: spirit pins it at
;; old revisions, which the tool refuses to bump (a collected UnbumpablePin)
;; until full multi-pin awareness exists.
;;
;; persona is a configured consumer: it pins signal-router / signal-harness /
;; signal-frame and is the stale writer in the w46v skew (primary-w46v). It
;; belongs in the sweep so its contract pins converge with the other consumers.
;; router and message are configured too: persona's whole-engine gate builds the
;; router-daemon / message-router it launches from persona's flake inputs
;; persona-router / persona-message. Those inputs were normalized to github: form
;; (persona main ac629103), so the tool now discovers persona->router and
;; persona->message flake edges and repoints them to the router/message
;; synchronizer tips — carrying the launched daemons onto the same contract revs
;; persona is bumped to, which is what closes the w46v wire skew.

((GitHub LiGoldragon)
 /git/github.com/LiGoldragon
 [(signal-frame AtRoot)
  (signal-router AtRoot)
  (signal-harness AtRoot)
  (introspect AtRoot)
  (persona AtRoot)
  (router AtRoot)
  (message AtRoot)]
 (main synchronizer)
 (ClusterRole (NixBuilder (ClusterProposal /git/github.com/LiGoldragon/goldragon/datom.nota)))
 (WireExercising [daemon daemons socket sockets wire])
 (synchronizer synchronizer@criome.net))
